            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-82560",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Pod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhausti ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Pod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhaustion formatting a POD document whose =over nesting drives the margin to the output width.\n\nEach =over adds its indent to the margin, which wrap() subtracts from the output width to get the space available for text. When that space reaches zero, the line-splitting substitution matches the empty string, and the loop consumes no input while appending the margin padding on every pass.\n\nFormatting an attacker-supplied POD document never returns, and the output grows until memory is exhausted."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82560",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: perl-base\nFixed Version: 5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.7\nLink: [CVE-2026-82560](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82560)\nPod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhaustion formatting a POD document whose =over nesting drives the margin to the output width.\n\nEach =over adds its indent to the margin, which wrap() subtracts from the output width to get the space available for text. When that space reaches zero, the line-splitting substitution matches the empty string, and the loop consumes no input while appending the margin padding on every pass.\n\nFormatting an attacker-supplied POD document never returns, and the output grows until memory is exhausted.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-82560**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|perl-base|5.38.2-3.2ubuntu0.7|[CVE-2026-82560](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-82560)|\n\nPod::Text versions before 6.1.1 for Perl allow CPU and memory exhaustion formatting a POD document whose =over nesting drives the margin to the output width.\n\nEach =over adds its indent to the margin, which wrap() subtracts from the output width to get the space available for text. When that space reaches zero, the line-splitting substitution matches the empty string, and the loop consumes no input while appending the margin padding on every pass.\n\nFormatting an attacker-supplied POD document never returns, and the output grows until memory is exhausted."
              },
